(4911148, 712708, 97166, '<td valign="top">Hello. I am making a point on commenting on the photos that I rated a 2 or 3 in this challenge.<br/> <br/>I gave this image a 3 for the following:<br/> <br/>I''m not sure if this was a shot taken from a long distance away and cropped in really, really tight, or if the camera optics just aren''t very good, but whatever the case the image suffers from bad artifacting, and what looks like blur/camera shake.  It also doesn''t have a very exciting composition.  <br/> <br/>If this was taken from far away and then cropped a lot, might I suggest getting closer next time if possible, or finding subjects that you can get closer to.  (If it''s just bad optics, well, can''t help there).<br/> <br/>As for composition, try finding angles that flatter the subjects more. Something where their heads aren''t hidden, or their expressions can come into play, or the body language can speak to the viewer.  Take your time and wait for the subjects to be more active.  Use props/food/etc. to get them to be more active (if allowable). <br/> <br/>This meets the challenge, yes, but for me it just has too much wrong with it to compete.</td>', 'Hello. I am making a point on commenting on the photos that I rated a 2 or 3 in this challenge. I gave this image a 3 for the following: I''m not sure if this was a shot taken from a long distance away and cropped in really, really tight, or if the camera optics just aren''t very good, but whatever the case the image suffers from bad artifacting, and what looks like blur/camera shake.  It also doesn''t have a very exciting composition.   If this was taken from far away and then cropped a lot, might I suggest getting closer next time if possible, or finding subjects that you can get closer to.  (If it''s just bad optics, well, can''t help there). As for composition, try finding angles that flatter the subjects more. Something where their heads aren''t hidden, or their expressions can come into play, or the body language can speak to the viewer.  Take your time and wait for the subjects to be more active.  Use props/food/etc. to get them to be more active (if allowable).  This meets the challenge, yes, but for me it just has too much wrong with it to compete.', '2008-08-25 23:07:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(4911149, 713553, 82707, '<td valign="top">Very cute!  Nice detail and colours!</td>', 'Very cute!  Nice detail and colours!', '2008-08-25 23:07:05.000000', NULL, 1),
