(4921443, 713730, 93411, '<td valign="top">horse  (hôrs)<br/> <br/>a. A large hoofed mammal (Equus caballus) having a short-haired coat, a long mane, and a long tail, domesticated since ancient times and used for riding and for drawing or carrying loads.<br/>b. An adult male horse; a stallion.<br/>c. Any of various equine mammals, such as the wild Asian species E. przewalskii or certain extinct forms related ancestrally to the modern horse.<br/>2. A frame or device, usually with four legs, used for supporting or holding.<br/>3. Sports A vaulting horse.<br/>4. Slang Heroin.<br/><b><i><u>5. Horsepower. Often used in the plural.</u></i></b> <br/>6. Mounted soldiers; cavalry: a squadron of horse.<br/> <br/> <br/>MEETS CHALLENGE TO ME!!!! COOL SHOT!</td>', 'horse  (hôrs) a. A large hoofed mammal (Equus caballus) having a short-haired coat, a long mane, and a long tail, domesticated since ancient times and used for riding and for drawing or carrying loads.b. An adult male horse; a stallion.c. Any of various equine mammals, such as the wild Asian species E. przewalskii or certain extinct forms related ancestrally to the modern horse.2. A frame or device, usually with four legs, used for supporting or holding.3. Sports A vaulting horse.4. Slang Heroin.5. Horsepower. Often used in the plural. 6. Mounted soldiers; cavalry: a squadron of horse.  MEETS CHALLENGE TO ME!!!! COOL SHOT!', '2008-08-30 13:20:15.000000', NULL, 1),
