(4925804, 712268, 59029, '<td valign="top">Lol Leenie, 1s and 2s will creep their way into your scoring histogram no matter how hard you try - but you have the right attitude!</td>', 'Lol Leenie, 1s and 2s will creep their way into your scoring histogram no matter how hard you try - but you have the right attitude!', '2008-09-01 14:33:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4925813, 713685, 50641, '<td valign="top">Nice panning!  Love the motion blur on the trees and the two other cars.  I do like this as is, but since I''m a processing junkie, I might also try a black layer or a vignette layer (blended with overlay, linear dodge, something funky) - just to make it look meaner and subdue the sunlight.  Anyway, sorry your pic got dinged by the dingbats ;-)</td>', 'Nice panning!  Love the motion blur on the trees and the two other cars.  I do like this as is, but since I''m a processing junkie, I might also try a black layer or a vignette layer (blended with overlay, linear dodge, something funky) - just to make it look meaner and subdue the sunlight.  Anyway, sorry your pic got dinged by the dingbats ;-)', '2008-09-01 14:34:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4925858, 713770, 59029, '<td valign="top">Liberty, so many of my early entries were incredibly oof and blurry, so that forced me to learn to shoot so my pix weren''t either.  Maybe all you need is a tripod or a faster shutter speed.</td>', 'Liberty, so many of my early entries were incredibly oof and blurry, so that forced me to learn to shoot so my pix weren''t either.  Maybe all you need is a tripod or a faster shutter speed.', '2008-09-01 14:44:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4925864, 713601, 50641, '<td valign="top">On Golden Pony.  The Gilded Gelding!  Striking warm tones.  Usually yellow makes things look gummy (in my hands anyway!)- but you''ve got a very sharp picture here nonetheless.  Great, especially considering it''s at 2.8 - and that depth of field makes for a nice immediate drop off to blur behind the horse.  Enjoyed.</td>', 'On Golden Pony.  The Gilded Gelding!  Striking warm tones.  Usually yellow makes things look gummy (in my hands anyway!)- but you''ve got a very sharp picture here nonetheless.  Great, especially considering it''s at 2.8 - and that depth of field makes for a nice immediate drop off to blur behind the horse.  Enjoyed.', '2008-09-01 14:45:07.000000', NULL, 0),
